"""Neuron hunt v2: gradient-attribution candidates, generation only (judging happens offline with Claude).

STAGE = "controls":
  1. persona (system-prompted) + neutral responses on DISC_Q
  2. attribution: d/d(dose) of mean per-token log p(persona response | no system prompt), minus the same for the
     neutral response, for every MLP neuron at once (one backward pass per batch). This is a first-order estimate of
     exactly what steering does, unlike run 1's activation-difference ranking, which found "reading" neurons.
  3. drop neurons that rank high for many concepts, screen top N_CAND per concept x DOSES x SCREEN_Q prompts
STAGE = "finals": generate FINALS configs on all EVAL_Q x 2 samples.

Steering recipe (from @_lyraaaa_): add dose * median(||resid|| leaving layer L) / ||W_down[:, n]|| to neuron n's
activation at the down_proj input, at every position.
"""
